          "dir": "T17",
          "file": "90161Z-T17-solution-test-a-r5.zip",
          "note": "You import test solution A r5 and run its flow (about 5 minutes, an estimate). A r4 failed in R18; r5 copies the layout of your R18 export (the connection is no longer a root component, the publisher matches yours).",
          "marker": "90161Z-T17-solution-a-started.txt",
          "url": "https://make.powerautomate.appsplatform.us/",
          "url_source": "Microsoft Learn, Power Automate US Government (https://learn.microsoft.com/power-automate/us-govt): DoD maker portal; editable in the window, remembered in Config (agent value, PFM to confirm in R13)",
          "urlConfig": "90161Z-flow-portal.txt",
          "guide": [
            "1. Select Open in browser. Power Automate opens; sign in with your CAC if asked.",
            "2. Leave older test solutions (\"90-161.Z solution import test A\" or \"... test B\") in Solutions: the import replaces A.",
            "3. Select Solutions (under More if you do not see it), then Import solution > Browse.",
            "4. In the File name box press Ctrl+V (the file path is on the clipboard), select Open, then Next.",
            "5. Connections: for SharePoint pick your existing connection. Select Import.",
            "6. Wait for \"Successfully imported\" (1-3 minutes, an estimate). Open the solution \"90-161.Z solution import test A\",",
            "   open the flow \"90161Z T17 Solution Import Test A r5\", select Run, paste the new site address into \"Site address\", then Run flow.",
            "7. Come back here and select \"Done: the run has started\".",
            "If the import fails: select Download log file (save it in any folder: the next step finds it), type the first line of the red error message (no names or site address) into the box below, then select It failed."
          ],
          "needs": [
            "net-flow",
            "flow-guide"
          ],
          "estimate": 5
        },
